WEBVTT

00:08:59.103 --> 00:09:00.650
So now that we know about this,

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:02.307
how do we combat it?

00:09:02.307 --> 00:09:03.929
And there are different avenues.

00:09:03.929 --> 00:09:05.363
One avenue is to appeal

00:09:05.363 --> 00:09:07.409
to people's emotional responses,

00:09:07.409 --> 00:09:09.542
to appeal to people's empathy,

00:09:09.542 --> 00:09:11.415
and we often do that through stories.

00:09:11.415 --> 00:09:13.980
So if you are a liberal parent

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.852
and you want to encourage your children

00:09:15.852 --> 00:09:18.226
to believe in the merits of nontraditional families,

00:09:18.226 --> 00:09:20.499
you might give them a book like this.
["Heather Has Two Mommies"]

00:09:20.499 --> 00:09:22.225
If you are conservative and have a different attitude,

00:09:22.225 --> 00:09:24.156
you might give them a book like this.

00:09:24.156 --> 00:09:25.905
(Laughter)
["Help! Mom! There Are Liberals under My Bed!"]

00:09:25.905 --> 00:09:29.241
But in general, stories can turn

00:09:29.241 --> 00:09:31.473
anonymous strangers into people who matter,